<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Release entitlements — H-07 / M-07.

	This file is new because there was nothing to add to. CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS
	was not set on EITHER build configuration, so exchangapay.entitlements was an
	orphan: it existed on disk, and Xcode never read it. The shipped app therefore
	carried no entitlements at all — no aps-environment, which is why push could
	only ever have worked by accident, and no associated-domains, which is the
	iOS half of M-07.

	Two files rather than one, because aps-environment is the one entitlement that
	must genuinely differ per configuration:

	  exchangapay.entitlements         Debug    aps-environment = development
	  exchangapayRelease.entitlements  Release  aps-environment = production

	A Release build signed with `development` connects to Apple's sandbox APNs.
	Tokens minted there are silently rejected by the production gateway, so push
	fails for every user in a way that looks like a backend fault. The [H-07]
	build phase asserts this file says `production`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>

	<!--
		M-07: Universal Links for the OAuth callback.

		Both tenants are listed on purpose. iOS ignores an applinks domain that
		does not resolve for this app, so an unmatched entry is inert rather than
		an error — and PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER is currently com.exchangapay.tst
		in the Release configuration, so listing only the prod domain would leave
		Universal Links dead in exactly the build this file governs.

		REQUIRES, or the build will not sign:
		  1. Associated Domains enabled on the App ID at developer.apple.com
		  2. provisioning profiles regenerated afterwards
		  3. Team ID + bundle ID registered in the Auth0 Dashboard, so Auth0
		     serves the apple-app-site-association file

		See security/M07_APPLINKS_SETUP.md.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:exchangapay.eu.auth0.com</string>
		<string>applinks:exchangapay-tst.eu.auth0.com</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
